WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.240 --> 00:00:01.910 align:start position:0%
 
ever wonder what extreme lengths your  favorite actors had to go to for a role  acting may look easy but many actors  have put themselves through a lot for  their characters  for example did you know that kate  winslet had to learn to hold her breath  for  over seven minutes it's safe to say that  acting requires  more than just looking good on camera i  don't know if i'd go through  this one again in an interview with gq  jacob belordy shared that he had to  learn how to ride a motorcycle for his  role  in the kissing booth he said while  shooting in south africa he was  basically thrown onto a motorcycle on  the side of a freeway  and was told to just figure it out he  said he fell a lot but  it was an awesome experience i don't  ride them my mum won't let me  in order to convincingly play olympic  figure skater tanya harding  margot trained for three months prior to  shooting she worked with skating  choreographer sarah kawahara  training about four times a week  starting completely from scratch  margo learned to spin a little bit  they started out with stretching then  practiced choreography on the floor  and eventually moving to the ice getting  on the ice i was like  i'm gonna break something and if i break  something i'm doing the maths in my head  i'm like it would cost us  how much robert pattinson's upcoming  version of batman has the actor working  under a grueling training regimen  it's required him to train in various  forms of martial arts  and he's becoming pretty skilled in  jiu-jitsu it's been reported that we  will get to see his version  of batman as a full force fighting  machine  and that robert has really been putting  the work in  gal gadot's training for wonder woman  required her to train  six hours a day six months before  shooting began  it was two hours of gym work two hours  of fight choreography and one and a half  to two hours  learning how to horseback ride she was  genuinely surprised at how painful it  was learning how to ride horseback and  she has a new respect for those who do  it regularly  i've learned how to fight with swords  horseback riding which is very  challenging  and a lot of hours in the gym in an  interview with us today  timothy shared that he spent about a  month and a half training to sword fight  and ride horses  while wearing the incredibly heavy armor  he would be wearing in the film  he said it was to get him into a place  that he looked like he could  convincingly  hold his own in a battle you try to get  good on the horse too  try to get good on a horse while  wielding a sword that kind of thing  in an interview with seth meyers ansel  revealed that he took about 10 stunt  driving classes in preparation for his  role as baby  he said he was able to do most of the  stunts after taking the classes but  while filming with his co-stars jamie  foxx and jon hamm  he wasn't allowed to drive he was  allowed to do some of the stunts when it  was just him though  oh interesting yeah so they didn't want  to risk the whole cast  yeah just me just part of it yeah  in the upcoming avatar 2 kate plays a  water person  which requires her to perform scenes  underwater in an interview with the  hollywood reporter kate said i had to  learn how to free dive to play that role  in avatar  and that was just incredible my longest  breath hold was 7 minutes and 14 seconds  like crazy crazy stuff madeleine has  aquaphobia  which is a fear of natural bodies of  water that made shooting her scene of  falling through the ice in season one  incredibly difficult she said that the  tank she was in for shooting was so deep  she couldn't see the bottom or the scuba  divers in the corner ready to jump in if  something happened  [Music]  jennifer said she loved her trainer and  she was incredibly strict  she said if i had a bad form she would  pinch my ear  she really didn't put up with anything  jennifer revealed that the training  permanently changed her bodies  my shoulders were two inches broader and  my right arm is one inch longer than my  left arm  the arrows weighed like two pounds right  i would like aim and look all cool and  then i'd shoot it and i'm just going  poop yifei leo was already an  accomplished martial artist before  landing mulan  but she still had to undergo six to  seven hours of training a day for three  months before shooting  she became skilled in wushu which is a  contemporary form of chinese martial  arts  cinematographer mandy walker said she  did 90  of her own stunts in the movie i wanted  to see  how much more i can do as an actress  while the actor isn't generally known as  a method actor he did learn how to make  the certain substance walter white was  famous for  he revealed on the graham norton show  that he spent time at the drug  enforcement agency where the chemist  there  showed him how to create the stuff he  said it was very interesting  intricate and dangerous and it's a  massive experience emotionally and  physically  joseph gordon-levitt actually had an  eight-day intense training session with  the person he was portraying in the walk  philippe petit before shooting  eventually he was able to walk across a  wire that was two feet off the ground  with ease  during his time with him he also learned  how to ride a unicycle  and to walk on his hands from fatigue  what i've learned is the balance comes  much  easier being in motion john went through  rigorous military-based training for his  role in 13 hours  in addition to spending countless hours  in the gym to get in shape he learned  several skills to make him feel like a  soldier  he had weapons training tactile training  and even learned how to maneuver through  a burning building  how many hours in the gym it was about  three to four hours a day for six days a  week and  yes yes it is there it is that is not  fake  leo went above and beyond for the  revenant including being close to death  several times  he had to sleep in animal carcasses go  in and out of freezing water  and eat raw animal meat including bison  liver  for the graphic bear fighting scene leo  said that it involved a lot of cables  and intense choreography yes it was  incredibly difficult to do  but you know we rehearsed for for weeks  beforehand on just that sequence  olivia went through extensive training  for her role in x-men  mainly learning sword fighting she  trained for five months  six hours a day learning how to  effortlessly and safely wield a katana  sword  it paid off because she ended up doing  95  of her own stunts in the film i've never  done sword work before and i started  doing  all the sword work and then wire and  stunt training  natalie portman spent eight hours a day  training as a ballerina for black swan  that paired with her extreme diet of  basically almonds and carrots  the oscar winner said she thought she  was going to die she even dislocated her  rib in rehearsals  but said that's not uncommon for  ballerinas to hurt themselves during the  process  i had to train a year before the film  so it it was great to sort of immerse  myself in everything  halle berry is now known as the best  female weapons handler in hollywood  due to her dedication for john wick in  preparation for the role she trained  with tar and tactical  she confessed that her training was the  hardest six to seven months of her life  she also became skilled in martial arts  and dog training  and even had three broken ribs during  that time i don't think she ever missed  a workout in the five months  since being cast in the new rocky creed  franchise michael b  jordan has spent years honing his boxing  skills even telling tmz  that he could hold his own against  former world champion roy jones jr  that definitely takes some guts but it's  impressive that michael has taken his  training for the franchise so seriously  the internet's boyfriend keanu reeves  actually had to learn how to surf for  point break  learning from the surf doctor of  hollywood dennis jarvis  dennis said that the training lasted for  about two months before shooting  and that all of the actors were pretty  much beginners keanu took such a shine  to surfing  that dennis made him his own custom  surfboard for personal use  for his role in fury shia labeouf joined  the national guard during the filming  process  spending a month living on a military  base while on the military base he  became a chaplain's assistant  he also went to extreme lengths outside  of the military training  he had a tooth fold and would cut a scar  into his face  after watching these actors push their  limits and train for months  we are truly impressed by the dedication  they have to their craft having to look  like a master of these insane skills  while being fully in character is  clearly what sets these actors in a  class of their own  learning a new skill or hobby is hard  enough let alone with a whole cast crew  and  studio watching to make sure you nail it  this definitely  makes us want to re-watch all of these  movies now

